## 2. STRIDE Analysis

| Category | Threat | Mitigation | Residual Risk |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Spoofing | A container on the `services` network impersonates a legitimate caller | Network segmentation; JWT verification at the gateway (P6.2) | <!-- TODO(scaffold) --> |
| Tampering | Results or events are altered in transit or at rest | Hash chain in the ledger (P3.7), consensus voting (P4.5), schema validation (P3.1) | <!-- TODO(scaffold) --> |
| Repudiation | An operation cannot be traced to a task | Structured logs with `taskId` and `traceId` (CLAUDE.md 6.1) | <!-- TODO(scaffold) --> |
| Information Disclosure | Database credentials leak | Credentials from env, moved to OpenBao in P5.3; `.env` git-ignored | <!-- TODO(scaffold) --> |
| Denial of Service | A large addition exhausts memory or CPU | `mem_limit` and `cpus` per container; rate limits at the gateway (P6.2) | <!-- TODO(scaffold) --> |
| Elevation of Privilege | A compromised process gains host access | Non-root user in the runtime image; minimal base image | <!-- TODO(scaffold) --> |

